  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-railist",
      "text": "**English** | [中文](#中文)\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "English",
      "text": "Manage the whole DSH left column as one list: reorder rows across the panel list and the footer action row, rename them, change their icons, hide them, and fold them into Groups. Everything is configured in a new Settings tab and applies immediately.\n\n> A fork of [dsh-panellist](https://github.com/qwq1999/dsh-panellist). Upstream manages the panel list alone; this fork extends it to a single sequence spanning two seats.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **One sequence across seats** — the panel list and the footer action row are sorted as a single list, so a row can be dragged from one into the other.\n- **Reorder by drag** — drag any row to a new position; the rail follows the list live.\n- **Rename and re-icon** — give any row your own label and pick its icon from a built-in set.\n- **Show / hide** — take a row off the rail without uninstalling its plugin.\n- **Groups** — fold several rows into one Group row with a flyout menu; ungroup at any time.\n- **Appearance override** — adjust the rail's own look from the Settings tab.\n- **Config file's full path** — shown in Settings so you can back it up or edit it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "The Settings row itself always stays last and cannot be dragged, and every change is written to disk only when you press Save."
    },
    {
      "section": "Screenshots",
      "text": "| Settings → Panel list | Appearance override | A Group menu on the rail |\n| :-: | :-: | :-: |\n|  |  |  |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-railist\n```\n\nThen restart DSH. To remove it:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-railist\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "| Requirement | Version |\n| --- | --- |\n| DSH | `>=0.2.0-rc.2 <0.3.0-0` |\n| Node | `^22.19.0 \\|\\| >=24.0.0` |\n| Profile | `web` |\n| Platform | Windows / macOS / Linux desktop |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Your settings live in `~/.dsh/railist.json`. The full path is also shown in the Settings tab. If a row's plugin is missing or disabled, the row is kept in the file and marked as missing rather than being deleted."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "中文",
